Thus, the legal principles discernible from the aforesaid decision of this Court may be summarised as under:--
(a) Vicarious liability can be fastened on those who are in-charge of and responsible to the company or firm for the conduct of its business.
For the purpose of Section 141, the firm comes within the ambit of a company;
(b) It is not necessary to reproduce the language of Section 141 verbatim in the complaint since the complaint is required to be read as a whole;
